<l n="191">Longo tempore diſposui </l>
<l n="192">mori lacerarunt florem </l>
<l n="193">Argiuorum. poſtquam uerò </l>
</lg>
<lg n="199-200">
<l n="194">Acris hyemis alia machinatione grauiore, primatibus </l>
<l n="195">Vates clanxit proſtrens </l>
</lg>
<lg n="202-204">
<l n="196">Dianam, ut terram </l>
<l n="197">Fuſtibus concutientes Atride </l>
<l n="198">Non continuerint lachrymas. </l>
</lg>
<lg n="205-210">
<milestone unit="card" n="205" resp="Smyth"/><l n="199">Rex uerò ſenex hoc dixit clamans: </l>
<l n="200">Grauis Parca non creditu est, </l>
<l n="201">Grauis uerò,ſi </l>
<l n="202">Natam opprimam domorum effigiem. </l>
<l n="203">Inquinans iugulatis uirginis </l>
</lg>
<pb n="132"/>
<lg n="211-213">
<l n="204">Fluentis paternas manus. </l>
<l n="205">Prope aram, ſine his </l>
<l n="206">Malis, fic defertor nauis ero, </l>
<l n="207">Aberrans à focietate. </l>
</lg>
<lg n="214-217">
<l n="208">Quiescente uerò facrificio, </l>
<l n="209">E' uirgineo ſanguine </l>
<l n="210">Ira,iratè cupere </l>
<l n="211">Fas, bene enim erit </l>
</lg>
<lg n="218-221">
<milestone unit="card" n="218" resp="Smyth"/><l n="212">Poſtquam neceßitatis ſubijt uinculum </l>
<l n="213">Mentis fpirans impiam mutationem, </l>
<l n="214">Impura profanamq unde audace ſapientia mutauit </l>
<l n="215">Mortalibus, audebat enim turpitudo </l>
</lg>
<lg n="223-225">
<l n="216">Mifera, amentia, præcipuum nocumentum. </l>
<l n="217">Tolerabat igitur facrificulus </l>
<l n="218">Fieri filiæ muliere laboriofo </l>
<l n="219">Bello auxiliator, principią nauium </l>
</lg>
<lg n="228-229">
<milestone unit="card" n="228" resp="Smyth"/><l n="220">Preces &amp; fortes paternas </l>
<l n="221">Nihil pependerunt uitam uirgineam pugnæ cupidi arbitris. </l>
</lg>
<lg n="231-232">
<l n="222">Dixit uerò sacrificiis pater post preces, </l>
<l n="223">Inſtar Chimæræ ſuper aram </l>
</lg>
<lg n="233-235">
<l n="224">Peplis procidentem omni animo </l>
<l n="225">Et procumbentem ut acciperent ſublimi, </l>
<l n="226">Pulchri orisque </l>
</lg>
<lg n="236-237">
<l n="227">Custodiam obtinerent, </l>
<l n="228">Sonum horridum domi, </l>
<milestone unit="card" n="238" resp="Smyth"/><l n="229">Vi frenorum, multo animi robore. </l>
</lg>
<lg n="239-241">
<l n="230">Croci colorem in campum fundens, </l>
<pb n="133"/>
<l n="231">Eiecit quemq; ſacrificorum ab oculos iaculo </l>
<l n="232">Lugubri, decens ut in tabulis loqui </l>
<l n="233">Volens ſæpiſsime postquam </l>
</lg>
<lg n="244-245">
<l n="234">Patris iuxta uiriles conuiuas </l>
<l n="235">Debuit caſta ſine iugo loquutio </l>
<l n="236">Patris chari beatum ter confæderatum </l>
</lg>
<lg n="246-249">
<l n="237">Seculum charè honorabat. </l>
<l n="238">Que uerò inde, neq; noui, neq; dicam, </l>
<milestone unit="card" n="248" resp="Smyth"/><l n="239">Techne Calchamis non imperfect ſunt. </l>
<l n="240">Pena hos dolentes discere propendit </l>
</lg>
<lg n="252">
<l n="241">Futura: hoc uerò audire, </l>
</lg>
<lg n="253">
<l n="242">Poſtquam fiet expiatio, ualeat. </l>
</lg>
<lg n="254">
<l n="243">Aequale uerò </l>
</lg>
<lg n="255">
<l n="244">Manifestum fatum ueniet uerum cum ipfis. </l>
</lg>
<lg n="256-257">
<l n="245">Fit uerò in his bonum opus, </l>
<l n="246">Vt uult hoc proximum Apiæ </l>
</lg>
<lg n="258">
<milestone unit="card" n="258" resp="Smyth"/><l n="247">Terræ munitum uallum. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="258-260">
<l n="248">Venio colens Cytemnestra tuum robur. </l>
<l n="249">Iustum est uirum principem honorare </l>
<l n="250">Vxorem relicto folio uirili. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cly.</speaker>
<lg n="261-263">
<l n="251">Tu uerò siue bonum, fiue non audiens </l>
<l n="252">Nuncia ſpe placabis. </l>
<l n="253">Audirem lata,neq; taceat inuidia, </l>
</lg>
<lg n="264-265">
<l n="254">Nuncius bonus quide queadmodu ſe habet puerbili, </l>
<l n="255">Fiat à matre nocte,dics. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>NVN</speaker>
<lg n="266-267">
<l n="256">Intelliges gaudium maius ſhe audire. </l>
<l n="257">Priami occuparunt Argiui urbem. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <pb n="134"/>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cly.</speaker>
<lg n="268-269">
<l n="258">Qua dicis aufugit fermo pre incredulitate, </l>
<l n="259">Troiam exiftentem Achæoru, manifeſtè dico. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="270-271">
<l n="260">Gaudium me inuadit, euocata ad lachrymas. </l>
<l n="261">Bene enim tui ſapiemis oculus comprobat. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cly.</speaker>
<lg n="272-273">
<l n="262">Quod'nam fidele tibi est fignum horums </l>
<l n="263">Hoc est, nisi Deus me decipiat. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="274-275">
<l n="264">Vtru uifiones fomniorŭ colis faciles perfuafu? </l>
<l n="265">Non opinionem acciperem torpeſcětis mentis. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cly.</speaker>
<lg n="276-277">
<l n="266">Sed te premit aliqua bene alata fama? </l>
<l n="267">Tang uuenis pueri ualde reprehendiſti mente. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="278">
<l n="268">Quo tempore uaſtata eſt urbs? </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cly.</speaker>
<lg n="279">
<l n="269">Lucem huius parientis noctis dico. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="280">
<l n="270">Et quis nunciorum uenit ita celeriter? </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cly.</speaker>
<lg n="281">
<milestone unit="card" n="281" resp="Smyth"/><l n="271">Vulcanus ex Ida lucidum mittens iubar, </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <lg n="282-285">
<l n="272">Splendorem ſplendor huc à nuncio ignis </l>
<l n="273">mifit, Ida quidem ad cumulatum promontorium </l>
<l n="274">Lemni, magnam uifionem ex inſula tertium </l>
<l n="275">Athoon cacumn Iouis fufcepit, </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="286-288">
<l n="276">Perfecta ut peragraret pontum, </l>
<l n="277">Violenta eur,tis flammæ ad uoluptatem </l>
<l n="278">Teda, aureum tanquam ſal </l>
<l n="279">Jubar nuncians Maciſti ſcopulis, </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="290-291">
<l n="280">Que neq; cunctans, neq; occupata tanquam ſomno </l>
<l n="281">Victa, tranfiuit partem nuncij </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="292-293">
<l n="282">Procul uerò flamme lumen in fluentis Euripi </l>
<l n="283">Mesapij cuſtodi ſignificat ueniens. </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="294-295">
<l n="284">Hi uerò contrà fplenduerunt, </l>
<l n="285">núnciarunt ulterius </l>
</lg>
        <pb n="135"/>
        <lg n="295-296">
<l n="286">Terre, erice accruum accendentes igni. </l>
<l n="287">Firmata fax nequaquam obſcurata, </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="297-298">
<l n="288">Tranfiliens campum Oropi, inſtar </l>
<l n="289">Clare lunæ ad Cithæronis promontorium, </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="299">
<l n="290">Excitauit aliam ſequelam deducentis ignis. </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="300-301">
<l n="291">Lux longè deducens non recuſauit, </l>
<l n="292">Custodia plus incendere quàm quæ dicta ſunt. </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="302-304">
<l n="293">Stagnum fupra Gorgopem illuftrauit lumen, </l>
<l n="294">Perueniensq ad montem Argioplanctum, </l>
<l n="295">Iußit inftitutum non indulgere igni. </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="305-309">
<l n="296">Mittunt uerò Androntes ingentifortitudine, </l>
<l n="297">Magnam ignis flammam: Saronici </l>
<l n="298">Freti ſpeculum &amp; non ulterius ſuperare </l>
<l n="299">Flammantem, deinde colluſtrauit:deinde appulit </l>
<l n="300">Arachneum cacumen, urbi uicinos ſcopulos. </l>
</lg>
        <lg n="310">
<l n="301">Et deinde in hanc domum Atridarum insiliuit, </l>
</lg>
        <sp>
    <speaker>[Kly.]</speaker>
<lg n="1066-1068">

<gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="9" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:311-319"/><milestone unit="card" n="320" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="35" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:320-354"/><milestone unit="card" n="355" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="12" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:355-366"/><milestone unit="card" n="367" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="18" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:367-384"/><milestone unit="card" n="385" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="18" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:385-402"/><milestone unit="card" n="403" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="17" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:403-419"/><milestone unit="card" n="420" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="17" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:420-436"/><milestone unit="card" n="437" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="19" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:437-455"/><milestone unit="card" n="456" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="19" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:456-474"/><milestone unit="card" n="475" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="13" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:475-487"/><milestone unit="card" n="488" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="50" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:488-537"/><milestone unit="card" n="538" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="45" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:538-582"/><milestone unit="card" n="583" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="30" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:583-612"/><milestone unit="card" n="613" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="23" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:613-635"/><milestone unit="card" n="636" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="45" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:636-680"/><milestone unit="card" n="681" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="18" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:681-698"/><milestone unit="card" n="699" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="17" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:699-715"/><milestone unit="card" n="716" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="11" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:716-726"/><milestone unit="card" n="727" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="10" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:727-736"/><milestone unit="card" n="737" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="13" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:737-749"/><milestone unit="card" n="750" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="13" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:750-762"/><milestone unit="card" n="763" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="9" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:763-771"/><milestone unit="card" n="772" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="10" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:772-781"/><milestone unit="card" n="782" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="28" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:782-809"/><milestone unit="card" n="810" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="45" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:810-854"/><milestone unit="card" n="855" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="32" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:855-886"/><milestone unit="card" n="887" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="27" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:887-913"/><milestone unit="card" n="914" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="30" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:914-943"/><milestone unit="card" n="944" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="31" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:944-974"/><milestone unit="card" n="975" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="13" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:975-987"/><milestone unit="card" n="988" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="13" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:988-1000"/><milestone unit="card" n="1001" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="16" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1001-1016"/><milestone unit="card" n="1017" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="18" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1017-1034"/><milestone unit="card" n="1035" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="31" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1035-1065"/><l n="302">Priusquam sanguineum ſpumaret robur. </l>


<l n="303">Non tamen plus proijciens ſpernar. </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp><speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1068-1071">
<l n="304">Ego uerò miſereor, non irafcar. </l>

<l n="305">Ito ô mifera hoc uehiculum relinquens, </l>
<l n="306">Lubens neceßitas hoc iugum nuncia huic </l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1072-1073">
<milestone unit="card" n="1072" resp="Smyth"/><l n="307">Oto totote, pope, da. ò Apollo Apollo.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1074-1075">
<l n="308">Quid talia uociferata es ad Loxiam?</l>
<l n="309">Non enim talis est ut exaudiat lamentationem.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1076-1077">
<milestone unit="card" n="1076" resp="Smyth"/><l n="310">Ototota, papada,</l>
<l n="311">O' Apollo, Apollo.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1078-1079">
<l n="312">Certè rursus malè ominans Deum inuocat.</l>
</lg>
<pb n="136"/>
<lg n="1079-1082">
<l n="313">Nihil accedentem in luctu adeffe.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1080-1082">
<milestone unit="card" n="1080" resp="Smyth"/><l n="314">Apollo, Apollo.</l>
<l n="315">Agyeu Apollomi</l>
<l n="316">Perdidifti, non uix ſecundo.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1083-1084">
<l n="317">Flere uidetur pro fuis malis.</l>
<l n="318">Expectat numen unum apud mentem feruilem.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1085-1087">
<milestone unit="card" n="1085" resp="Smyth"/><l n="319">Apollo, Apollo.</l>
<l n="320">Agyeuq; Apollo mi,</l>
<l n="321">Quónam tandem duxisti me,</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1087">
<l n="322">Ad quam domum?</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1088-1089">
<l n="323">Ad Atridas, ſi tu cogitas,</l>
<l n="324">Ego dico tibi, hæc non dices mendacia eſse.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1090-1092">
<milestone unit="card" n="1090" resp="Smyth"/><l n="325">Heuheu. Deo inuisam igitur, multa conſcia</l>
<l n="326">Cruenta mala appendere,</l>
<l n="327">Viri, uidimam &amp; campum aspersum.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1093-1094">
<l n="328">Videtur ſagax hospita canis instar</l>
<l n="329">Eſse, uaticinatur ex quibus inueniat cædem.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1095-1097">
<milestone unit="card" n="1095" resp="Smyth"/><l n="330">Teſtibus his objequor,</l>
<l n="331">Flensq; hos pueros, cedesq;</l>
<l n="332">Apparentes &amp; carnes à patre uoratas.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1098-1099">
<l n="333">Audiuimus tuam laudem ſatidicam.</l>
<l n="334">Attamen nullos uates perſcrutamur.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1100-1104">
<milestone unit="card" n="1100" resp="Smyth"/><l n="335">Heu pape, quid tandem curat,</l>
<l n="336">Quid tandem nouus dolor magnus,</l>
<l n="337">Magnumn in ædibus his curat malum</l>
<l n="338">Non finendum amicis,</l>
</lg>
<pb n="137"/>
<lg n="1105-1106">
<l n="339">Curatu difficile ſubſidium</l>
<l n="340">Procul uerò abest.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1105-1106">
<l n="341">Horum inſcius sum uaticiniorum,</l>
<l n="342">Illa uerò noui, omnis ciuitas clamat.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1107-1111">
<milestone unit="card" n="1107" resp="Smyth"/><l n="343">Heu misera, hoc enim facis</l>
<l n="344">Coniugem maritum</l>
<l n="345">Lauacris purgans,</l>
<l n="346">Quomodo finem dicam?</l>
<l n="347">Celer</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1111">
<l n="348">Extendere manum ex</l>
<l n="349">Manu expetens.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1112-1113">
<l n="350">Nondum intellexi.</l>
<l n="351">Nunc enim ex enigmatis</l>
<l n="352">In obſcuris oraculis hæsito.</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1114-1115">
<milestone unit="card" n="1114" resp="Smyth"/><l n="353">Heuheu, papa pape.</l>
<l n="354">Quid hoc apparet?</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1115-1118">
<l n="355">Rete ſanè Plutonis.</l>
<l n="356">Sed rete coniux &amp; in cauſa erit</l>
<l n="357">Cædis, ſeditio immoderata eſt.</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1118-118">
<l n="358">Eiulet perniciosum facrificium.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1119-1124">
<l n="359">Quam furiam ad ædes uocat?</l>
<l n="360">Vastans me non iſte ſermo exhilarat.</l>
<l n="361">Per cor cucurrit croco tincta</l>
<l n="362">Gutta, Doriaq; eſt caduca.</l>
<l n="363">Occurrit uitæ potens radijs.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1124">
<l n="364">Celer uerò nocumentum eſt.</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1125-1129">
<milestone unit="card" n="1125" resp="Smyth"/><l n="365">Heu, ecce, ecce,</l>
<l n="366">Auerte à boue</l>
<l n="367">Taurum, in peplis</l>
<l n="368">Nigra cornua accipiens machinamento</l>
<l n="369">Percutit, proijcit in uas humidum,</l>
</lg>
<pb n="138"/>
<lg n="1129-1130">
<l n="370">Decipientis lebetis,</l>
<l n="371">Fortunam tibi dico.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1130-1131">
<l n="372">Non iacutarem ſummi fatidicarum ſententiaru</l>
<l n="373">Eſse, huic malo hæc afsimilabo.</l>
<l n="374">Mortalis aliqua bona fama</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1134-1135">
<l n="375">Per mala enim</l>
<l n="376">Multiloque fortunæ</l>
<l n="377">Fatidicum metum</l>
<l n="378">Ferunt intelligere.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1136">
<milestone unit="card" n="1136" resp="Smyth"/><l n="379">Hei miseræ</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1136-1138">
<l n="380">Infelices sunt fortunæ.</l>
<l n="381">Meum enim narrat</l>
<l n="382">Dolorem effundens.</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1138-1139">
<l n="383">Quid me huc miferam duxiſti</l>
<l n="384">Una occisam nihil tandem sum.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1140-1145">
<l n="385">Mente capta numine afflata pro ipſa dicis</l>
<l n="386">Legem iniquam. tanquam mulis insatiata boas: hei</l>
<l n="387">miseræ mente, Ityn Ityn lugens florentem malis</l>
<l n="388">Luscinia uita.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1146-1149">
<milestone unit="card" n="1146" resp="Smyth"/><l n="389">Heu heu canoris luſcinia fatum</l>
<l n="390">Circundederunt alatum corpus</l>
<l n="391">Dij, dulceq; euum ſemotum à luctibus.</l>
<l n="392">Me uerò ſpectat discisio ancipiti haſta.</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <sp>
<speaker>Cho.</speaker>
<lg n="1150-1155">
<l n="393">Vnde impetuosos Dei afflatos habes,</l>
<l n="394">Ac uanos mærores?</l>
<l n="395">Hæc præ nefando timore clangit, carmina ſimulas</l>
<l n="396">Orthijs incisionib. unde terminos habes fatidice vide</l>
<l n="397">Maledicos?</l>
</lg>
</sp>
        <pb n="139"/>
        <sp>
<speaker>Ca.</speaker>
<lg n="1156">
<milestone unit="card" n="1156" resp="Smyth"/><l n="398">Heuheu nuptie Paridis pernicioſæ</l>
</lg>
<lg n="1157-1159">
<l n="399">Amicis, heu potus patrius Scamandri.</l>
<l n="400">Tunc enim circa tuas ripas misera crescebam alimentis.</l>
<gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="7" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1160-1166"/><milestone unit="card" n="1167" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="11" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1167-1177"/><milestone unit="card" n="1178" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="24" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1178-1201"/><milestone unit="card" n="1202" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="40" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1202-1241"/><milestone unit="card" n="1242" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="53" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1242-1294"/><milestone unit="card" n="1295" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="36" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1295-1330"/><milestone unit="card" n="1331" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="12" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1331-1342"/><milestone unit="card" n="1343" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="1" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1343-1343"/><milestone unit="card" n="1344" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="1" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1344-1344"/><milestone unit="card" n="1345" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="1" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1345-1345"/><milestone unit="card" n="1346" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="2" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1346-1347"/><milestone unit="card" n="1348" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="24" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg005.perseus-grc2:1348-1371"/><milestone unit="card" n="1372" resp="Smyth"/><gap reason="omitted" unit="line" quantity="35" corresp="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0085.tlg